    <div class="guide-container">
    <div class="guide-hero">
      <h1>S-CORE User Guide</h1>
      <p>Everything you need to know to get your requests submitted and approved.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- 1. Getting Started -->
    <div class="guide-section">
      <div class="guide-section-header">
        <div class="guide-section-icon">
          <svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
            <circle cx="8.5" cy="8.5" r="1.5"></circle>
            <polyline points="21,15 16,10 5,21"></polyline>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h2>Getting Started</h2>
      </div>
      <p>Welcome to S-CORE! This is your official portal for all communication with the Strategic Communications Office (SCO). This guide will help you submit your requests correctly.</p>
      <div class="guide-image-placeholder" style="background: #f3f4f6; border: 2px dashed #d1d5db; border-radius: 8px; padding: 80px 20px; text-align: center; margin: 24px 0; color: #6b7280;">
        <svg width="48" height="48" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" style="margin: 0 auto 12px; opacity: 0.5;">
          <rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
          <circle cx="8.5" cy="8.5" r="1.5"></circle>
          <polyline points="21,15 16,10 5,21"></polyline>
        </svg>
        <p style="margin: 0; font-weight: 600;">Add Screenshot: User Dashboard</p>
      </div>
      <div class="guide-step">
        <h4>Your Dashboard</h4>
        <p>This is your command center. It shows you the real-time status of all your submitted requests and any recent activity.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="guide-step">
        <h4>Your Profile</h4>
        <p>Click your name in the top-right corner to go to your Profile. Please keep your contact information up-to-date.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="guide-step">
        <h4>Notifications</h4>
        <p>The bell icon shows you all updates, including when your request status changes or when an SCO member sends you a message.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 2. The Two Request Types -->
    <div class="guide-section">
      <div class="guide-section-header">
        <div class="guide-section-icon">
          <svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
            <path d="M6 8h12M6 12h12M6 16h12"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h2>The Two Request Types: What's the Difference?</h2>
      </div>
      <p>This is the most important rule. Choosing the wrong type will cause delays.</p>
      <div class="guide-step">
        <h4>
          <span style="vertical-align:middle; margin-right:8px;">
            <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v16a2 2 0 002 2h12a2 2 0 002-2V8z"></path>
              <polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"></polyline>
              <line x1="16" y1="13" x2="8" y2="13"></line>
              <line x1="16" y1="17" x2="8" y2="17"></line>
              <polyline points="10 9 9 9 8 9"></polyline>
            </svg>
          </span>
          Request for Approval
        </h4>
        <p><strong>What it is:</strong> Use this when you have already created a file and you need the SCO to review and officially approve it.</p>
        <p><strong>Examples:</strong> Submitting a final publication mat, asking for caption approval, or getting a project proposal signed off.</p>
        <ol style="margin-top:12px;">
          <li>Click <strong>Request for Approval</strong> in the sidebar.</li>
          <li>In the modal, enter a clear title and detailed description of your file and what needs approval.</li>
          <li>Select the approval type (e.g., Publication, Caption, Project Proposal).</li>
          <li>Set the priority and deadline (submit at least 3 working days in advance).</li>
          <li>Upload your file(s) for review (e.g., pubmat, document, caption).</li>
          <li>Review all details, then click <strong>Submit</strong>. Your request is now locked.</li>
          <li>If your status changes to <strong>For Revision</strong>, use the modal to upload new files and respond to feedback in the Conversation tab.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <div class="guide-step">
        <h4>
          <span style="vertical-align:middle; margin-right:8px;">
            <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <path d="M14.7 6.3a1 1 0 000 1.4l1.6 1.6a1 1 0 001.4 0l3.77-3.77a6 6 0 01-7.94 7.94l-6.91 6.91a2.12 2.12 0 01-3-3l6.91-6.91a6 6 0 017.94-7.94l-3.76 3.76z"></path>
            </svg>
          </span>
          Request for Service
        </h4>
        <p><strong>What it is:</strong> Use this when you need an SCO unit (like Graphics or Multimedia) to create a new file or deliverable for you.</p>
        <p><strong>Examples:</strong> Requesting a new logo, asking for a video to be filmed, or needing a new poster designed from scratch.</p>
        <ol style="margin-top:12px;">
          <li>Click <strong>Request for Service</strong> in the sidebar.</li>
          <li>In the modal, enter a clear title and detailed description of what you want created.</li>
          <li>Set the priority and deadline (submit at least 7 working days in advance).</li>
          <li>Attach any reference files, logos, or text needed for the task.</li>
          <li>Review all details, then click <strong>Submit</strong>. Your request is now locked.</li>
          <li>If your status changes to <strong>For Revision</strong>, use the modal to upload new files and respond to feedback in the Conversation tab.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 3. How to Submit a Request -->
    <div class="guide-section">
      <div class="guide-section-header">
        <div class="guide-section-icon">
          <svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
            <path d="M12 8v8M8 12h8"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h2>How to Submit a Request</h2>
      </div>
      <ul>
        <li>Click "Request for Approval" or "Request for Service" on the sidebar.</li>
        <li>Fill out the form with a clear and specific title and a detailed description. (e.g., "Need pubmat for 'CSO Week - Day 1'" is better than "Pubmat").</li>
        <li>Attach all necessary files.</li>
        <li>Click "Submit."</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="guide-image-placeholder" style="background: #f3f4f6; border: 2px dashed #d1d5db; border-radius: 8px; padding: 80px 20px; text-align: center; margin: 24px 0; color: #6b7280;">
        <svg width="48" height="48" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" style="margin: 0 auto 12px; opacity: 0.5;">
          <rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
          <circle cx="8.5" cy="8.5" r="1.5"></circle>
          <polyline points="21,15 16,10 5,21"></polyline>
        </svg>
        <p style="margin: 0; font-weight: 600;">Add Screenshot: A request form modal (Service or Approval)</p>
      </div>
      <div class="guide-warning">
        <strong>CRITICAL RULE:</strong> Once you click "Submit," your request is locked and cannot be edited. You can only upload new files if an SCO member sets your task status to "For Revision". Please double-check your submission before you submit it.
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- 4. Understanding Your Request Status -->
    <div class="guide-section">
      <div class="guide-section-header">
        <div class="guide-section-icon">
          <svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="6"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h2>Understanding Your Request Status</h2>
      </div>
      <p>Your dashboard will show the status of your tasks. Here is what they mean:</p>
      <div class="guide-image-placeholder" style="background: #f3f4f6; border: 2px dashed #d1d5db; border-radius: 8px; padding: 80px 20px; text-align: center; margin: 24px 0; color: #6b7280;">
        <svg width="48" height="48" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" style="margin: 0 auto 12px; opacity: 0.5;">
          <rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
          <circle cx="8.5" cy="8.5" r="1.5"></circle>
          <polyline points="21,15 16,10 5,21"></polyline>
        </svg>
        <p style="margin: 0; font-weight: 600;">Add Screenshot: Request status badges (Pending, In Progress, For Revision, etc.)</p>
      </div>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Pending:</strong> Your request has been submitted and is in the queue for an Admin to review and assign to a unit team.</li>
        <li><strong>In Progress:</strong> An SCO unit member has acknowledged your task and is actively working on it.</li>
        <li><strong>For Revision:</strong> <span style="color:#dc2626;font-weight:600;">ACTION REQUIRED.</span> An SCO member has reviewed your task and needs changes. You must check the Conversation tab to read their feedback. This is the only status that allows you to upload new files.</li>
        <li><strong>Approved:</strong> (For Approval Requests) Your submitted file has been reviewed and is officially approved. The task is complete.</li>
        <li><strong>Completed:</strong> (For Service Requests) The SCO unit has finished your task and uploaded the final file. Check the task details to download your deliverable.</li>
        <li><strong>Rejected:</strong> The request was not approved. Check the Conversation tab for the reason.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- 5. Notifications -->
    <div class="guide-section">
      <div class="guide-section-header">
        <div class="guide-section-icon">
          <svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <path d="M18 8A6 6 0 0 0 6 8c0 7-3 9-3 9h18s-3-2-3-9"/>
            <path d="M13.73 21a2 2 0 0 1-3.46 0"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h2>Notifications</h2>
      </div>
      <p>The bell icon is your most important tool for tracking progress. You will receive a notification when:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>An Admin or Unit Member sends you a new message in the Conversation tab.</li>
        <li>The status of your request changes (e.g., from "Pending" to "In Progress").</li>
        <li>A unit member uploads a final file for your Service Request.</li>
        <li>An Admin posts a system-wide announcement.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- 6. Best Practices -->
    <div class="guide-section">
      <div class="guide-section-header">
        <div class="guide-section-icon">
          <svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <polygon points="12,2 15.09,8.26 22,9.27 17,14.14 18.18,21.02 12,17.77 5.82,21.02 7,14.14 2,9.27 8.91,8.26"></polygon>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h2>Best Practices: The S-CORE Guidelines</h2>
      </div>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>SUBMIT EARLY!</strong> The SCO processes requests based on official timelines. Submitting a request "for tomorrow" will likely be rejected.</li>
        <li>Approval Requests: Submit at least 3 working days in advance.</li>
        <li>Service Requests: Submit at least 7 working days in advance.</li>
        <li><strong>BE DETAILED.</strong> Provide clear titles, detailed descriptions, and attach all necessary files (logos, text files, photos) in your first submission. This prevents delays.</li>
        <li><strong>USE THE CONVERSATION TAB.</strong> This is your only official channel for communicating about a task. Do not rely on email. Use the Conversation tab to ask questions, respond to feedback, and get updates.</li>
        <li><strong>CHECK "FOR REVISION" TASKS.</strong> If you see a task is "For Revision," your action is required. Open the task, read the feedback in the Conversation tab, make the changes, and upload your new file.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>




    <!-- Quick Access Shortcuts (Moved to End) -->
    <div class="guide-section">
      <div class="guide-section-header">
        <div class="guide-section-icon">
          <svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"></path>
            <path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></path>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h2>Quick Access</h2>
      </div>
